  "notes": "Transcribed from the official SCC 'Railroad Operations A.S. Degree - Cohort 2 - Cal-GETC GE (Fall Start)' program map, Catalog 2026-27, published August 14, 2026 (mapmaker.losrios.edu/Maps/7801/PublishedPdf). Start Term: Fall. GE Pattern: Cal-GETC. Official Total Units: 60-61; this seed models the first-listed/recommended path = 15 + 12 + 6 + 13 + 14 = 60 units (ENGL C1000 at 3 units per the official SCC English course page). Semester sums verified against the map's 15-16 / 12 / 6 / 13 / 14 headers. Unlike Cohort 1 (map 7798), Cohort 2 front-loads GE in Semester 2/Spring and runs the RAILR sequence in Summer/Fall. Choice slots: (1) GE ENGL C1000 / H 488 / ESLW 340, Area 1A — ENGL C1000 selected; (2) Elec INDIS 313 / HCD 310 — INDIS 313 selected. In-plan prereqs: RAILR 140 requires RAILR 120 and 122 with grades of 'C' or better; RAILR 142 requires RAILR 120, 122, and 140 with grades of 'C' or better. Documented: students not placing directly in ENGL C1000 take the ENGL 80/ENGL C1000 combo; ENGL 488 requires ESL 325; ESLW 340 requires ESL 325 or Los Rios assessment placement; students not placing directly in MATH 300 take the MATHS 95/MATH 300 combo. Area 4 rule: Cal-GETC Area 4 requires 2 courses from different disciplines — the Sem 4 Area 4 course must differ from the Sem 1 Area 4 course. GE Area 5C: the 1-unit Associate Lab Component is not required if a laboratory activity is included in the Area 5A or 5B course (per map note); modeled here as a generic 1-unit Area 5C slot. AA/AS requirements: 60 degree-applicable units with 2.0 GPA, 12 units within Los Rios, each required course 'C' or better, Cal-GETC Areas 1-6 with 'C' or better. Electives: any courses numbered 100-499. Railroad Operations, Business & Industry Meta Majors. Exception: students with a BA/BS or higher from a CHEA-recognized accredited institution are deemed to have satisfied GE and graduation competency requirements. tccns mirrors SCC local course codes (California community colleges do not use TCCNS).",
